// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 12-type-system
// facility: rule.type.typing [T-If]
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// An `if` condition is a `bool`. The checker once discarded the result
// of checking a condition, so `if (5)` compiled under cobc and was
// caught only at run time by coby.

fn main()
{
    if (5)
    {
    }
}
